# Code owners for mcl-core.
#
# Every line here is a REVIEW requirement, not a claim of authorship. It takes
# effect only once branch protection requires code-owner review, which is
# applied after the repositories become public -- GitHub Free does not offer
# protection on a private repository.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the specific paths below override the
# catch-all.

#
# WHY THESE PATHS NAME TWO OWNERS AND NOT ONE.
#
# They named only @0j0bit until 2026-09-12. That deadlocks: GitHub does not let
# anyone approve their own pull request, and the branch ruleset grants no
# bypass to administrators, so a pull request touching one of these paths and
# authored by its sole code owner could never be merged by anyone. The first
# change to hit it would have been the one recording rows 27 and 37, which
# touches /governance/ and /releases/.
#
# Both named accounts have write access, which a code owner must have to count.
# These lines currently resolve to the same two people as the catch-all, so
# their present effect is documentary: they record which paths are authorities.
# If the catch-all ever widens, they narrow again on their own.

* @0j0bit @sed-boi

